From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TurboVadim <yolkin.vadim@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:48:17 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Reuse spawning callbacks and stop blocked mob-cap scans

Use SpawnState as its predicate and completion callback, keep one player-count
callback per ChunkMap, and reuse a lazy start position after its coordinates
have been copied. Skip unused throttle math when throttling is disabled.

Read caps and player counters live, stop once minimum headroom is nonpositive,
and reuse nearby membership only across ordinary ArrayList categories that
cannot invoke spawn callbacks. Custom iterators still resolve every category.
Preserve category traversal, attempt decisions, RNG calls and listener effects.

The measured candidate also held a biome-lookup hint, dropped for having no
measured effect. It passed 13 focused tests and all seven behavior digest
checks. Six interleaved idle-survival runs per jar measured
9.616 -> 9.229 mspt, -4.03% +/- 6.89% at 95%, and 2313.704 -> 1936.051 KB/t,
-16.32% +/- 2.91%. Moving-player timing was +0.35% +/- 6.09%. These results
measure the combined candidate, not this patch in isolation.

